  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "Public omics archives and screening datasets are driving demand for faster, automated, single-command analysis tools that make reanalysis practical.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is re-engineering of established analysis steps for speed, automation, and usability rather than introducing new statistical methods. deepTools4 rewrites core functions of a genomic sequencing analysis suite, reporting benchmarked speed-ups and updated visualization. MAUDE-Py reimplements the MAUDE probabilistic framework in Python for sorting-based pooled CRISPR screens, adding automated baselines and null sampling. CLIPittyClip packages CLIP sequencing analysis as a local single-command pipeline from raw FASTQ to peak matrices and crosslink sites, with a 27-fold faster Python crosslink step. Meta2Data automates retrieval and processing of public microbiome data from INSDC and CNCB using DADA2 or VSEARCH. MetaHQ instead contributes harmonized metadata annotations across public omics samples and studies. The items span distinct domains, so this thread is dominant rather than shared by every item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
